1. mpv and Android JNI binding

   Source: https://github.com/Riteshp2001/mpvlibAndroid
   Fixed binding baseline: tag 2026-06-25
   Fixed binding commit: 168e0a5e43b37c85509050cddcb5eaddc2e313c0
   mpv source: https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv
   Fixed mpv commit: 2339eb72767517fc5a113283939f59076946fbc1
   mpv source identity: v0.41.0-dev-g2339eb727
   Embedded runtime string: mpv v0.41.0-774-g2339eb727
   FFmpeg source: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg
   Fixed FFmpeg tag: n9.0.1
   Fixed FFmpeg commit: bf1b838f2ab88b4f8fd83443325c782ea0e0f7fa
   Source closure AAR SHA-256: 7CB0B25DC15F21278992243CE2597193B7A54E1A488933555B572982203E2BC0

   Kiyori builds the complete arm64 player closure from these fixed sources,
   including the Java binding, libplayer JNI bridge, mpv, FFmpeg, Mbed TLS,
   libplacebo, shaderc, the matching libc++_shared.so, and required assets.
   The audited source AAR is transformed deterministically into the selected
   product AAR. To keep the HTTPS-capable player FFmpeg closure isolated from
   the application's FFmpegKit tools, Kiyori rewrites only equal-length ELF
   SONAME and DT_NEEDED strings and stores the seven FFmpeg libraries as
   libmpcodec.so, libmpdevice.so, libmpfilter.so, libmpformat.so, libmputil.so,
   libmpresample.so, and libmpscale.so. The native machine code and symbol
   implementations are not replaced. The selected ELF closure contains no
   RPATH or RUNPATH and all PT_LOAD alignments are at least 0x4000.
   Distribution must provide the complete corresponding source,
   transformation scripts, build information, and notices required by the
   applicable mpv, FFmpeg, Mbed TLS, and GPL licenses.

