3. FFmpegKit Maintained and FFmpeg

   Java/API compatibility baseline: dev.ffmpegkit-maintained:ffmpeg-kit-full:8.1.7
   Source: https://github.com/ffmpegkit-maintained/ffmpeg
   Fixed tag: v8.1.7
   Fixed tag object/commit: 62b07bf097baf26b416c815aea514e05c9ad6d63
   Kiyori wrapper version: 8.1.7-kiyori-n9.0.1-r4
   FFmpeg source: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg
   Fixed FFmpeg tag: n9.0.1
   Fixed FFmpeg commit: bf1b838f2ab88b4f8fd83443325c782ea0e0f7fa
   OpenH264 source: https://github.com/cisco/openh264
   Fixed OpenH264 tag: v2.6.0
   Fixed OpenH264 commit: 652bdb7719f30b52b08e506645a7322ff1b2cc6f
   Source AAR SHA-256: DF332D8F2FECA7508541A2F20EDB348A3BFBC2AD5AE6EEFDEDF2889D679C96CC

   Kiyori restores the fixed maintained framework source, applies the audited
   FFmpeg 9 host integration overlay, maps constrained baseline to OpenH264's
   baseline enum, applies the fixed BsFlush empty-word correction, and preserves
   an Android application's already-started Binder threadpool before transcode. It retains
   the Java API, proguard metadata, embedded res/raw license and source notices,
   and the nine FFmpegKit/FFmpeg libraries. The tools AAR omits its C++ runtime so
   the APK contains the unique matching runtime supplied by the player closure
   described above. These normal libav*.so names are loaded only by the
   non-exported :ffmpeg process; the main process uses Binder, and the :player
   process resolves only the namespaced mpv FFmpeg closure.

   Tools arm64 AAR SHA-256: 86D97CC0174FF44A8057899BEF7B8E66BD976E5CFA7BBA7D2A9FC819CB8EFCA7

   FFmpeg and enabled external libraries retain their own licenses.
   Distribution must provide relinkable/dynamically linked library materials
   and corresponding source as required by LGPL-3.0 and each enabled library's
